  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - aiomqtt's Client is fundamentally an async context manager (async with ... as client) tied to connect/disconnect 
lifecycle via __aenter__/__aexit__; paho's model of instantiate-then-call-.connect()-then-reuse-across-many-sync-method-calls 
has no structural equivalent.
    - All aiomqtt I/O operations (connect, publish, subscribe, etc.) are coroutines requiring `await` inside an async 
function/event loop; the TelemetryBridge class and its publish_reading/publish_batch methods are synchronous and 
dependency-injected as a plain client object with no async execution context, so bridging requires spinning up an event loop 
per call, which breaks connection persistence and defeats the purpose of the async context manager.
    - The DI pattern in the source (client created once in __init__, reused for many later synchronous publish calls) is 
incompatible with aiomqtt's scoping model, where the client/connection is only valid within the `async with` block; no wrapper
can safely keep the underlying connection open outside that block for arbitrary later synchronous calls.
    - aiomqtt.publish() returns None rather than an info object with .rc, so the wrapper can only fabricate a fake return 
value, not reflect genuine broker-side publish acknowledgement in a sync-compatible way.

